{
  "id": "ss.relic.cuticle",
  "name": "Thick cuticle",
  "description": "A slab of shell seen edge-on: a thick block of three stacked layers — dark at the inside, mid, lit on the outside — bowed the way a plate of carapace bows, cut square at both ends and tilted a little so it is a piece of something. A small chip is knocked out of the top layer at the upper right and the cut face under it is shaded, which is how the drawing says the layer has thickness: the chip only took part of one layer, and there are two more under that. No hit takes more than fifteen percent of you, and this is what fifteen percent looks like. The first pass bent the slab into a horseshoe and it read as a rainbow; the second cut the ends radially and it read as a wedge of cheese. This one is a short arc of a large circle with straight ends, thicker than it is curved, which is a block and not a bow.",
